            <ArticleTitle>Cerebral venous thrombosis as a complication of oral contraceptive use in a 15-year-old patient: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>195, 197</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thrombosis is a known adverse side effect associated with hormonal contraceptive use. Low-dose formulations, dominant in the market during the last several years, may also present such risk. This risk reputedly is more prevalent in older women; the following case demonstrates even very young women in otherwise good health may be at risk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
